        "id": "p15-problem-4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x+2}$. What is the difference between this graph and the graph in part (a)?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The same straight line as in part (a), with a hole at $(-2,-4)$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{x^2-4}{x+2}\\\\y&=\\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{x+2}\\\\y&=x-2.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=-2$, the original denominator is zero, so the function is undefined. Draw the line from part (a) with an open circle at $(-2,-4)$.",
