        "answer": {
          "short": "$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x+2},&x\\ne-2\\\\-4,&x=-2.\\end{cases}$$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-2$, the rational expression equals $x-2$. Fill the hole using the value of this line at $x=-2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-2)&=-2-2\\\\f(-2)&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nThus\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x+2},&x\\ne-2\\\\-4,&x=-2.\\end{cases}$$\nThis defines the same continuous line $y=x-2$ for every real $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
